## Rollback

If the deploy causes errors, roll back to the previous Container App revision:

```bash
# List recent revisions
az containerapp revision list \
  --name ca-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --resource-group rg-<%workload%>-<env> \
  -o table

# Activate previous revision
az containerapp revision activate \
  --name ca-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --resource-group rg-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --revision <PREVIOUS_REVISION_NAME>

# Deactivate bad revision
az containerapp revision deactivate \
  --name ca-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --resource-group rg-<%workload%>-<env> \
  --revision <BAD_REVISION_NAME>
```

For Function Apps, use deployment slots or re-deploy the previous image tag.

## Known failure modes

- **OIDC auth failure** (`AADSTS70021`): federated credential subject mismatch — check `docs/conventions/secrets.md` for exact subject format.
- **Bicep validation fails**: run `az bicep build --file infra/main.bicep` locally to surface errors before re-pushing.
- **Container App stuck in `Provisioning`**: check Application Insights and Container App system logs (`az containerapp logs show`).
- **Health check fails after deploy**: check that `FUNCTIONS_NODE_RUNTIME` (Functions) or the container image tag matches the deployed artifact.

